CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ const pack pattern preserved: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/8: pack expansion substitutes each element INTO the
pattern, cv-qualifiers included.  The in-class parameter-pack replication
used to replace the whole pattern type `const Es &` with the raw element,
dropping the const; the non-const `Es &` parameters could not bind rvalue
arguments ([dcl.init.ref]/5) and the only viable constructor vanished
("found no match for symbol 'Tup'", main truncated).  Root cause of the
libstdc++ make_tuple arity >= 3 failure (cpp17_tuple_basic).  Header-free;
g++/clang++ runtime-verified.
